  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p> You take a burst of shot to the solar plexus. One of the pellets penetrate further than its compatriots, holing something you’d rather keep intact… stomach content, gall, fecal matter or some other foulness start leaking into your abdominal cavity. Next stop peritonitis!</p> <p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Stunned] (3). You also contract Blood Rot. \n Unless you receive Surgery you won’t be able to recover two of your lost Wounds. \n If you’re singularly unlucky you’ll encounter a surgeon who will insist on testing his theories of digestion through the hole in your stomach before (maybe) sewing you up. (Note to GM: Look up the story of Canadian trapper Alexis St Martin for inspiration.)</p>"
    },
